# Site content punctuation

Do not use en dashes (`–`, U+2013) or em dashes (`—`, U+2014) in user-facing copy, SEO text, or content in `site.ts`.

Use instead:

- **Commas** for continuing clauses: "systems that work in the real world, from R&D through production"
- **Colons** to introduce a list or explanation: "Meet the culture behind AIT: collaborative teams"
- **Periods** to split related sentences: "You are not just writing code. You are building something durable."
- **Regular hyphens** (`-`, ASCII) only for compound words and numeric ranges where appropriate (e.g. `on-site`, `770-672-0543`)

```typescript
// Bad
title: 'Test Engineer — LabVIEW & TestStand'
body: 'partner \u2014 delivering solutions'

// Good
title: 'Test Engineer, LabVIEW & TestStand'
body: 'partner, delivering solutions'
```

When editing `src/shared/content/site.ts`, keep all public strings free of `\u2013` and `\u2014` escapes.
